      "statement": "`grep` treats NUL-containing input as binary unless text mode is selected, supports skipping binary files, computes selections while suppressing ordinary binary rows, and maps final outcomes to 0 for a selection, 1 for no selection, and 2 for an error, with an explicit quiet match taking precedence over recorded errors.",
