      "statement": "`find` normally evaluates a visit before descending so `-prune` can block traversal, but `-delete` forces post-order depth-first evaluation; traversal also honors min/max depth, avoids descending symlinked directories, and processes deferred batches even after `-quit` unwinds traversal.",
